#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:1
msgid "AutoDD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:3
msgid ""
"AutoDD reduces a failing Python program while preserving a selected failure "
"signature. It repeatedly rewrites the program's Python abstract syntax tree "
"(AST), executes each candidate, and keeps candidates whose standard output "
"or standard error still contains the requested text. The result is a "
"smaller, standalone reproducer that is easier to inspect, report, and turn "
"into a regression test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:10
msgid ""
"AutoDD is intended for deterministic failures that can be reproduced by "
"running one Python file. It minimizes Python source, not TIR after lowering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:13
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:15
msgid ""
"First, run the source program directly and choose a short, stable, and "
"specific substring from its output. Then invoke AutoDD:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:18
msgid ""
"python -m tilelang.autodd examples/autodd/tilelang_buggy.py \\\n"
"  --err-msg \"T.gemm K shape check failed\" \\\n"
"  -o minimized.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:24
msgid ""
"Run the minimized file to confirm that it still exposes the intended failure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:26
msgid "python minimized.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:30
msgid ""
"AutoDD considers a candidate interesting when `--err-msg` occurs in captured "
"standard output or standard error. Matching is case-sensitive and does not "
"require a nonzero exit status. Use a distinctive failure substring so an "
"unrelated warning or log message cannot satisfy the test accidentally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:35
msgid "Command-Line Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/autodd.md:37
msgid ""
"python -m tilelang.autodd source --err-msg MSG -o OUTPUT \\\n"
"  [--backend {runner,subproc}] [--timeout SEC] [-j N]\n"
msgstr ""

